mob/proc/guidefile()
	src<<browse({"
<body bgcolor="#000000" text="#FFFFFF">
<font face="Tahoma">
<font color=silver style="font-size: 12pt">Newbie Guide</font>
<font style="font-size: 8pt">
<br>
<br>
<u>First of all:</u><br><br>

	In this game, verbs like Self Train and Focus Train are considered back up training methods.
The best way to train in this game is to go out and kill mobs. Not only does it give generous EXP and
zenni but it also adds to your skills, which has a great affect on your fighting abilities. For
example, two fighters with even stats may be evenly matched, but if one has maxed their Melee skill
and their opponent hasn't, they will easily defeat their opponent.

	Your Ki Control skill is your best skill overall. It not only affects your base stats
but also your stat multipliers in advanced forms like Super Saiyan, High Tension and Invert. The best way to
increase this skill is by powering up and down or Meditating on it. Shooting dummies and Transforming also increase this
skill. <br><br>

	All other skills can be trained in the gym. Melee is trained by hitting dummies, and this skill affects
not only physical damage and Strength, but it also determines defence output
(-25%). Shooting dummies increases Ki Use, Ki Power and Ki Control skills, all in that priority.
Deflect machines work your Ki Defense, Ki Resistance and Deflect skills. Counter Machines work your Defense, as
well as your Block, Dodge and Counter skills. Treadmills are the best way to increase your
stamina. Finally, Weights are the best way to increase your base strength.<br><br>

	Purchasing weighted clothing is one of the best ways to train. Each new peice you acquire
adds an extra multiplier onto your base EXP output when using training verbs. This explains why
they are so expensive.<br><br>

	Being born with a higher Warrior Level like Elite, Legend or God will grant the player higher
base stats. These ranks also determine chances of getting rare gene chromosomes.<br><br>

	All in all, overall stats do not account for much without your combat skills. Once skills are maxed,
players will then naturally rely on higher stats to dominate the game. <br><br>


<u>Training:</u> There are various ways to train in Ruination.<br><br>

Self Train<br>
Focus Train<br>
Dual Train<br>
Weighted Clothing<br>
Spar<br>
Gravity Train<br>
Hyperbolic Time Chamber<br>
Gym Train<br>
Defeat Sagas<br>
Defeat NPCs<br>
Defeat other players<br><br>

<u>Self Train:</u> Hit the 'Training' tab located at the top right corner
of your screen, and click 'Train'. Your character will start shadow boxing.
Self Train gives EXP, Training Points and Zenni. It's the most popular
training method in the game, although not as effective as killing NPCs.<br><br>

<u>Focus Train:</u> By concentrating on a certain stat, you can gain
more towards it. You do sacrifice some EXP, Training Points and Zenni,
but it can come in handy early in the game to focus on stamina, or in
the late game while focusing on Powerlevel or offensive/defensive stats.<br><br>

<u>Dual Train:</u> You need to have a partner for this training, so get
a friend, hit the 'Training' tab, located at the top right corner
of your screen, and click 'Dual Train'. Your partner must be 1 tile away
from you. Dual Train gives slightly more EXP than Self Train and Training
Points.<br><br>

<u>Weighted Clothing:</u> You can get weighted clothing from the Training
Shop Keepers a short stroll north-west of Yamcha in the gym. Weighted clothing
multiplies EXP received from Self/Focus Train. Every piece - and every tier
(standard, advanced, super, ultra) - adds more EXP, which is why they are so expensive.
<br><br>

<u>Spar:</u> Hit the 'Combat' tab located at the top right corner
of your screen, and click 'Spar'. You will toggle Spar mode.
You need a sparring partner and both of you must be in Spar mode. Keep
attacking each other to gain EXP and skills. Your characters won't deal much damage
since they are in Spar mode.<br><br>

<u>Gravity Train:</u> Gravity Pull rooms are currently undergoing maintenance and improvements.
Watch this space.<br><br>

<u>Hyperbolic Time Chamber:</u> HBTC is limited to 3 entries per character,
each visit being 400 minutes. It is recommended not to enter unless player has
all 8 peices of ultra weighted items plus weighted blade to get full EXP.
Waiting to go in is also a good thing in the late game because it becomes
hard to level up. Finally, since all you are going to do is self train...
AFK self training is allowed.<br><br>

<u>Gym Train:</u> You can also visit the Gyms located on several parts of
the map. At the Gym you may find some Dummies, Defense Machines, Weights,
Treadmills and Ki Machines. You can punch or shoot dummies to increase your
combat ability, both ki and melee. Weights raise your strength, Defense
Machines raise your defense. Treadmills raise your stamina, and Ki Machines
raise your ki defense.<br><br>

<u>Sagas:</u> You can either do it solo or create a party and team up on them.
If you go alone, you will get the EXP and Zenni boosts all for yourself, but if you
team up, everyone will get a piece of the pie.<br><br>

<u>NPCs:</u> Killing other NPCs like Green Saibaman, Demons or Super Saiyan 3s will
grant generous EXP and zenni. Coupled with shards this is easily the best form of
training in the game.<br>
<br>
Note: Killing mobs more than 20,000 levels lower than your own level will not contribute kill counts toward your reset counter.<br>
<br>

<u>Player vs Player:</u> You kill other players over level 2000 and gain EXP,
Zenni and possibly Z Points. If you're strong you may even get a place in
Ruination's Top 10. So train hard!
<br><br>
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<br><br>
<u>Training Attributes:</u> Training Points and Z Points.<br><br>
<u>Training Points:</u> Use them at {NPC}Yadrat Sensei for stat
boosts on Powerlevel, Ki, Ki Defense, Strength, Defense, and Stamina. They can
also add to your EXP or Speed.<br><br>
<u>Z Points:</u> Use them at {NPC}Yadrat Sensei to gain bonuses
to your stats as you level up. Bonus is a random integer from 50 to 75.
Strategic use comes in handy when using these points, as every Training Mode
adds a multiplier to this bonus. For example:
Mode (5) bonus = 50-75 x (5) + 1<br><br>
<br><br>
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
<br><br>
<u>Basic Stats:</u> Level, Powerlevel, Ki, Ki Defense, Strength, Defense, Speed, Fatigue<br><br>
<u>Skills:</u> Training Point Crit, Z Point Crit, Stat Crit, Transformation/Invert Skill,
Transformation/Invert Speed Melee, Block, Dodge, Counter, Critical, Durability,
Ki Control, Ki Power, Ki Use, Ki Resistance, Deflect, Weapon, Weapon Power, and
Weapon Resistance.<br><br>
<u>Level:</u> Your character's training level. Level determines how far you have trained.
Level is used for Technique requirements. The higher your Level, the higher your training
mode, and therefore the easier your stats will rise. Your Level will grow once your EXP
reaches 100%.<br><br>
<u>Powerlevel:</u> This is your character's health. Powerlevel influences melee damage
and defense, and is a requirement for <a href = ?TransFile>Transformations</a>.
Once your Powerlevel reaches 0, you will die or get knocked out.<br><br>
<u>Ki:</u> This is your character's energy. The higher your Ki, the more damage your
special techniques will cause.<br><br>
<u>Ki Defense:</u> Ki Defense is your character's defense against Ki attacks, such as Kamehameha etc.<br><br>
<u>Strength:</u> Strength is your character's attack power. The higher your strength, the more
melee damage you will cause.<br><br>
<u>Defense:</u> Defense is your character's defense against melee attacks. The higher your
Defense, the less damage you will take from melee attacks.<br><br>
<u>Speed:</u> How fast you can walk. This stat rises naturally as you level up.<br><br>
<u>Fatigue:</u> Your character's stamina. Once Fatigue reaches 100%, you will no longer be able to train,
therefore, you will not gain any EXP (however you may still kill NPCs and Players for EXP).
The treadmill is a good way to increase your Stamina. You can also concentrate on it
while you Self or Focus Train.<br><br>
<u>Training Point Crit:</u> A skill not used in combat. It is a chance to double training point gain.<br><br>
<u>Z Point Crit:</u> A skill not used in combat. It is a chance to double z point gain.<br><br>
<u>Stat Crit:</u> A skill not used in combat. It is a chance to strike an extra large stat gain while using
Self train or Focus train.<br><br>
<u>Melee:</u> Your ability to physically attack your opponent.<br><br>
<u>Block:</u> Your ability to block or deflect your opponent's melee attacks.<br><br>
<u>Dodge:</u> Your ability to Dodge your opponent's melee and Ki attacks.<br><br>
<u>Counter:</u> Your ability to Counter your opponent's melee attacks.<br><br>
<u>Critical:</u> Your ability to attack your opponent with more damage than your normal attack.<br><br>
<u>Durability:</u> Your ability to absorb physical attacks.<br><br>
<u>Ki Control:</u> This skill controls your overall power in all forms; base, Super Saiyan etc.<br><br>
<u>Ki Cast:</u> Your ability to cast ki attacks without them failing.<br><br>
<u>Ki Power:</u> This skill dictates the power of your energy attacks.<br><br>
<u>Ki Use:</u> This skill dictates how much ki you use for each energy attack.<br><br>
<u>Ki Resistance:</u> This skill determines you overall resistance or defense against ki attacks.<br><br>
<u>Deflect:</u> Your ability to Deflect your opponent's Ki attacks.<br><br>
<u>Weapon:</u> Your ability to attack using a weapon or weapon technique.<br><br>
<u>Weapon Power:</u> This skill determines the damage output of your weapon and weapon techniques.<br><br>
<u>Weapon Resistance:</u> Your ability to absorb weapon attacks and weapon techniques.<br><br>
<a href=?src=\ref[usr];action=Main>Main Guide Menu</a>
"})

