mob/proc/faqfile()
	src<<browse({"
<body bgcolor="#000000" text="#FFFFFF">
<font face="Tahoma">
<font color=silver style="font-size: 12pt">Frequently Asked Questions</font>
<font style="font-size: 8pt"><br><br>
Q: How many remakes are allowed per day?<br>
A: 5.<br><br>
Q: When do I learn power up?<br>
A: Level 1,000.<br><br>
Q: When do I learn Instant Transmission?<br>
A: Level 1,500.<br><br>
Q: What does "Concentrate" do?<br>
A: Concentrate is a feature that allows you to focus your training on one specific stat i.e.
Self train and Focus Train generate random stats, but by using concentrate you can focus on one
stat instead of all.<br><br>
Q: What should I concentrate on?<br>
A: Because combat drains stamina, veterans always concentrate on stamina first.<br><br>
Q: What does "Focus Train" do?<br>
A: Focus train is a verb that sacrifices a little bit of EXP, Zenni and TPs for a higher stat gain.
Combined with concentrate it can be a helpful verb, but is more geared toward the late (high
level) game.<br><br>
Q: Why won't my ki attacks work?<br>
A: You must increase your Ki Cast skill. Ki Cast = % of chance to cast ki moves.<br><br>
Q: Why do my stats start to decrease after I power up?<br>
A: Power up is a temporary function; ultimately it is your Ki Control skill that determines
stats in all forms. So If Ki Control = 50, Base stats = 50%.<br><br>
Q: How can I get zenni?<br>
A: You obtain small amounts of zenni from Self Train and Focus train, and larger amounts from
killing mobs and sagas. You also get half of whatever zenni someone is holding when you kill
them (a good reason to remember to bank your zenni periodically!).<br><br>
Q: Where can I buy weighted clothing?<br>
A: At the Training Shop Keepers, all of whom are a short north-west walk from Yamcha inside the gym.<br><br>
Q: Why are weights so expensive?<br>
A: Weights are not cheap because every regular weight adds 100% EXP bonus from self train
and focus train. With tiers going all the way up to Ultra (400%), they are expensive for a
reason.<br><br>
Q: How do I raise my rank?<br>
A: By killing mobs such as Saiyan Warriors, Angels, Demons, Saibamen etc.<br><br>
Q: What Mobs should I killed first?<br>
A: Green Saibamen, then Lesser Angels/Demons.<br><br>
Q: When do I get my first trans/invert?<br>
A: Check the transformation chart in the game guide.<br><br>
Q: What is Training Point Crit?<br>
A: A non-combat skill used to get double training points from verbs and mobs.<br><br>
Q: What is Z Point Crit?<br>
A: A non-combat skill used to get double z points from levels and players.<br><br>
Q: What is Stat Crit?<br>
A: A non-combat skill used to get extra large stat increases from Self train and Focus train.<br><br>
Q: Where can I increase these skills?<br>
A: Mr. Popo will increase these skills incrementally in exchange for zenni.<br><br>
Q: What are Z Points?<br>
A: Z Points (ZPs) add a bonus onto your stat of choice. A number will appear next to the stat in parentheses
(for example '(500)'), and you will gain this number in that stat each time you level up..<br><br>
Q: Where can I use my Z Points?<br>
A: You can use your ZPs at Yadrat Sensei, energy code 4239989.<br><br>
Q: What is the best stat to use ZPs on?<br>
A: Putting ZPs into EXP is usually a good move as this helps with leveling up quicker early in the game.
Otherwise, ZPs should be placed into stats that reflect your character build and what kind of fighter you
wish to be.A ki based fighter doesn't need to overload his strength, and vice versa.<br><br>
Q: When should I use my Z Points?<br>
A: Because higher training modes mean higher ZP bonuses, most veterans wait to use their
ZPs until a new training mode is attained. For example, level 70,000 = Demi-God; level 100,000 = Immortal.
A player at level 90,000 is likely to save their ZPs until Immortal mode for a juicier gain.<br><br>
Q: What are shards?<br>
A: There are two types of shards in the game; Training shards and Stat shards. They come in four different
sizes, each providing a larger bonus than the previous: small, large, great, and massive. Training shards may be
bought from the weighted clothing vendors and they have a limit of 20 uses. They add a bonus to your EXP, Stats
or Zenni for three hours, or until you log out. You can also obtain one permanent massive shard for EXP, Stats and
Zenni, which each add a 200% bonus to your training verbs permanently. However, these are very expensive/hard to
come by.<br>
<br>
Stat shards cannot be bought. They must be found by killing mobs. They add a permanent increase to your stats, once
again in four varying sizes which determine what % of your stats is added. You are allowed 10 stat shard uses, so
it's wiser to use only Massive shards if you can find them. Because these are a permanent increase, they are more
effective when you have higher stats.<br><br>
Q: Where can I buy a dragon radar?<br>
A: Misc. shop keeper, next to the weighted clothing vendors. Dragon radars only work for the earth Dragonballs and
require an upgrade from Bulma before being able to locate Namek or Black Star Dragonballs.<br><br>
Q: When is it best to use my wishes?<br>
A: Some start at Level 10,000, others at 100,000. Experimentation sometimes proves to be effective. As with ZPs,
wishes provide a better return if you have a higher training mode.<br><br>
Q: What should I use my wishes on?<br>
A: Use all of your wishes on Z Points to be one of the strongest players.<br><br>
Q: How can I get karma?<br>
A: By killing mobs, sagas or players. You can wish for karma, but wishes are limited and shouldn't be used
wastefully.<br><br>
Q: Why don't I have my transform/invert power verb?<br>
A: You don't get the verb until you reach the requirement(s).<br><br>
Q: How can I raise my transformation skill/speed?<br>
A: Skill is passively increased by staying transformed, and both skill and speed increase from
the transformation itself. Otherwise you can use the Meditate verb found in the training tab to
increase these skills.<br><br>
Q: When should I enter the HBTC?<br>
A: You should at least wait until after level 18,000. Using it early will give a good boost, but it will
effect you in the long run. Some players wait until after level 100,000 before entering. You have 3 entries.<br><br>
Q: How long can I stay in the HBTC?<br>
A: 400 minutes per use.<br><br>
<a href=?src=\ref[usr];action=Main>Main Guide Menu</a>
"})
